\section{Module 4: Persistent Storage \& Snapshot Disaster Recovery}

\subsection{Objective \& Storage Architecture}
Cloud computing decouples ephemeral compute nodes from persistent state. Module 4 implements a hybrid storage model combining:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Object Storage (Swift):} Highly scalable, RESTful storage for unstructured static assets and source code bundles.
    \item \textbf{Block Storage (Cinder):} High-performance, POSIX-compliant block devices attached to compute instances for stateful data execution.
    \item \textbf{Disaster Recovery (Snapshot Lifecycle):} Point-in-time snapshotting enabling volume replication and recovery on independent compute instances.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Swift Object Storage Setup}
A dedicated Swift container was initialized to store application source code:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Container Creation:} Container \texttt{module4-tetris-src} was provisioned with \texttt{Policy-0} and public read access (\nolinkurl{Read-ACL=.r:*}) enabled.
    \item \textbf{Object Upload:} Static web application source \texttt{index.html} (247 bytes) was uploaded into the container (Figure~\ref{fig:m4_swift_upload}).
\end{itemize}

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.88\linewidth]{img/m4-swift-container-object-upload.png}
\caption{Swift container \texttt{module4-tetris-src} storing \texttt{index.html} with public read ACL.}
\label{fig:m4_swift_upload}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Cinder Volume Integration \& Web Deployment}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Volume Provisioning \& Attachment:}
    A 1 GiB Cinder volume named \nolinkurl{module4-data-volume} was created and attached to \texttt{module3-web-sever}, recognized by the guest hypervisor driver as \texttt{/dev/vdc} (Figure~\ref{fig:m4_cinder_volume}).
    
    \item \textbf{In-Guest Filesystem \& Ingestion (Figure~\ref{fig:m4_vm1_workflow}):}
    Inside the instance, the volume was formatted and populated from Swift:
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash, basicstyle=\ttfamily\scriptsize]
$ sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/vdc
$ sudo mkdir -p /mnt/data && sudo mount /dev/vdc /mnt/data
$ cd /mnt/data
$ sudo wget http://192.168.2.10:8080/v1/AUTH_.../module4-tetris-src/index.html
\end{lstlisting}

    \item \textbf{Service Execution:}
    The web daemon was bound to the Cinder mount point:
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash, basicstyle=\ttfamily\scriptsize]
$ sudo busybox httpd -f -p 80 -h /mnt/data &
$ curl http://127.0.0.1
\end{lstlisting}
    Verified valid HTML content served directly from the persistent block device.
\end{enumerate}

